From 2a4cb3f6e6f0ea254792f3084c7ea8f2269bd591 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 03:51:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/11] perf(sim): B2 G1 traffic: split the remaining long
 pieces, refit cost()

From the G1 dense1m runs (headless, from load and in the warm window):

- the candidate radix sort runs in pieces (scan + max, histograms, per
  pass prefix + scatter by key ranges): one call was up to 8.4 ms cold;
- the snapshot's chunk plan (BuildingSnapshot.planBegin / planRun), the
  job clusters, the transfer CSR, the inbound fills / search start, the
  per-cycle origin arrays, the freight truck times and the transport
  save's build (installed by the cycle's last piece) get their own pieces;
- each sub-state of the big piece dispatchers is its own small method
  (design R10);
- every non-search loop uses half INFRA_PIECE_COLD_MS: those loops run
  once per cycle or per matching round and stay 10-37 x cold in days
  0-80 after a load (the accept loop ~45 x on its first executions);
  shop origins move to the cold budget;
- TC refit per piece label (late-window medians), SB searches get their
  own per-node cost, and one absolute scale TR_EST = 0.79 makes the
  estimates honest warm ms without moving a chunk.

Every split runs the same statements in the same order: frozen-original
and b2Pieces exactness pass at all piece scales. b2Pieces adds the O4
check (piece sequence and results identical with frames active or not).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KT9tXthEhyzExdUuGEecAJ
